{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**The problem.** You're hiking across a grid of `heights`, from the top-left cell to the bottom-right, moving up, down, left or right. A route's **effort** is the largest height difference between two consecutive cells on it. Return the minimum effort needed to cross."
    },
    {
      "type": "drawing",
      "src": "/drawings/5d468082-b360-424e-8334-e02a0303098a.svg",
      "alt": "A 3 by 3 height map. The green route goes down the left side and along the bottom: 1, 3, 5, 3, 5. Every step changes height by 2, so its effort is 2. The 8 in the middle, in red, would cost a step of 6.",
      "width": 514,
      "height": 316,
